## Dry Run of Key Functions

### Insert at Beginning (`insertAtBeginning(&head, 10)`)
- Head = NULL  
- Create new node: `[10 | NULL]`  
- `newNode->next = *head` → `[10 | NULL]` (next = NULL)  
- `*head = newNode` → head points to `[10]`  

Result:  
```
head → [10 | NULL]
```

---

### Insert at End (`insertAtEnd(&head, 20)`)
- List = `10`  
- Create `[20 | NULL]`  
- Traverse until last (`10`)  
- Attach → `10 -> 20`  

Result:  
```
head → [10 | next] → [20 | NULL]
```

---

### Insert at Position (`insertAtPosition(&head, 30, 3)`)
- Current list = `10 -> 20`  
- Position = 3 → stop at position 2 (node with `20`)  
- New node = `[30 | NULL]`  
- `newNode->next = temp->next` → `[30 | NULL]`  
- `temp->next = newNode`  

Result:  
```
10 -> 20 -> 30
```

