Alright Boss 💯 — now let’s move to **DELETE operations** in the same simple style.  
We’ll cover **all three delete cases** (just like we did insert):  

1. **Delete at Beginning**  
2. **Delete at End**  
3. **Delete at Position (Nth node)**  

---

## 🔹 Delete at Beginning
```c
void deleteAtBeginning(struct Node **head) {
    if (*head == NULL) {
        printf("List is empty!\n");
        return;
    }
    struct Node *temp = *head;   // store current head
    *head = (*head)->next;       // move head to next node
    free(temp);                  // free old head
}
```

👉 Steps:  
- Keep pointer to old head.  
- Move head to next node.  
- Free old head (so memory isn’t wasted).  

---

## 🔹 Delete at End
```c
void deleteAtEnd(struct Node **head) {
    if (*head == NULL) {
        printf("List is empty!\n");
        return;
    }
    if ((*head)->next == NULL) {   // only 1 node
        free(*head);
        *head = NULL;
        return;
    }

    struct Node *temp = *head;
    while (temp->next->next != NULL) { // stop at second last
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    free(temp->next);   // free last node
    temp->next = NULL;  // mark new end
}
```

👉 Steps:  
- Special case: if only one node → free it, head = NULL.  
- Otherwise: stop at **second last node**.  
- Free last node, set `secondLast->next = NULL`.  

---

## 🔹 Delete at Position (Nth node)
```c
void deleteAtPosition(struct Node **head, int position) {
    if (*head == NULL) {
        printf("List is empty!\n");
        return;
    }

    struct Node *temp = *head;

    // Case 1: delete first node
    if (position == 1) {
        *head = temp->next;
        free(temp);
        return;
    }

    // Move to (position-1)th node
    for (int i = 1; i < position - 1 && temp != NULL; i++) {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    if (temp == NULL || temp->next == NULL) {
        printf("Position out of range!\n");
        return;
    }

    struct Node *delNode = temp->next;
    temp->next = delNode->next;  // unlink node
    free(delNode);
}
```

👉 Steps:  
- If position = 1 → same as deleteAtBeginning.  
- Otherwise: move to node just before the one we want to delete.  
- Change its `next` to skip the unwanted node.  
- Free the unwanted node.  

---

